WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:19.760
Good afternoon ladies and gentlemen,
I last communicated with you on Monday&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:24.320
to express our serious concerns&nbsp;
regarding the intention of AstraZeneca&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:31.040
to supply considerably fewer doses in the coming weeks than agreed and announced.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:35.200
Since then we have been making all&nbsp;
efforts to resolve the situation.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:41.840
We convened a third meeting of the Steering Board on Monday night which resulted again in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:47.680
insufficient explanations from the company and&nbsp;
deep dissatisfaction among the Member States.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:56.720
Now let me be crystal clear: the 27 European&nbsp;Union Member States are united that AstraZeneca&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:02.160
needs to deliver on its commitments&nbsp;
in our agreement. We are in a pandemic.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:10.560
We lose people every day. These are not numbers. They are not statistics. These are persons, 

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:19.920
with families, with friends and colleagues that are all affected as well. Pharmaceutical companies,

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:26.960
vaccine developers, have moral, societal and contractual responsibilities, which they need to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:35.440
uphold. The view that the company is not obliged to deliver because we signed a ‘best effort' agreement

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:43.680
is neither correct nor is it acceptable. We signed an Advance Purchase Agreement for a product which&nbsp;

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:51.760
at the time did not exist and which still today&nbsp;is not yet authorised. And we signed it precisely

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:58.000
to ensure that the company builds a manufacturing&nbsp;capacity to produce the vaccine early so 

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:03.600
they can deliver a certain volume of doses&nbsp;the day that it is authorised. The logic of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:10.640
these agreements was as valid then as it is now. We provide a de-risking investment up front, in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:16.960
order to get a binding commitment from the company&nbsp;to pre-produce, even before it gets authorisation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:24.000
Not being able to ensure manufacturing capacity&nbsp;
is against the letter and the spirit of our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:32.000
agreement. We reject the logic of first come, first served. That may work at the neighbourhood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:37.840
butchers, but not in contracts. And not in our Advance Purchase Agreements.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:42.320
There's no priority clause in the Advance Purchase Agreement.

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:47.920
And also no there is also no hierarchy&nbsp;
of the four production plans named in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:54.080
the Advance Purchase Agreement. Two are in the&nbsp;located in the EU and two are located in the UK.

00:02:55.840 --> 00:03:01.200
Now We intend to defend the integrity of our investments and the taxpayers' money that has been&nbsp;

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:08.080
invested. We remain always open to engage with the company to resolve any outstanding issues in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:15.200
spirit of true collaboration and responsibility. That was always the spirit of our engagement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:24.720
with vaccine manufacturers since last spring. This&nbsp;evening, at 18.30, the Steering Board will convene

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:35.280
again. I call on Astrazeneca to engage fully, to&nbsp;rebuild trust, to provide complete information and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:43.440
to live up to its contractual, societal and moral&nbsp;obligations. Thank you very much.&nbsp;

